        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "composeFromObject"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "COMPOSEFROMOBJECT",
          "id": "1764154613207",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764154613208_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Role\nYou are an AI assistant responsible for drafting a {{$context.$variables.currentMode}}.\n\nYou are drafting this {{$context.$variables.currentMode}} from the Agent to the Customer, based on:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nUse the entire Reference Conversation only for factual grounding.\n\nYour output must ALWAYS follow the rules below. If ANY rule would be violated, you must FIX the output before returning it.\n\n## Reference Conversation (context)\nUse all content from:\n{{$context.$nodes.CREATECOMPOSECONTEXT.$output.result}}\n\nThis object may contain:\n- Messages (ordered by CreationDate)\n- Title\n- Problem Description\n- Additional metadata\n\nTreat this ONLY as background context. NEVER restate or summarize it.\n\n---\n\n## HARD RULES (STRICT — DO NOT BREAK)\n\n### 1. Tone\nIdentify tone from:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nApply it consistently throughout the output.\n\n### 2. Roles\n- SENDER: Agent  \n- RECIPIENT: Customer \n- Role labels, names, and sign-offs are NOT fixed literals and MUST be translated. \n\n### 3. MODE ENFORCEMENT (NO EXCEPTIONS)\n\nThe current mode is provided by:\n{{$context.$variables.currentMode}}\n\nYou MUST apply the correct rule based on its EXACT value:\n\n#### When currentMode is \"Email\":\n- You MUST begin the output with:\n  Subject: <short clear subject>\n- Then write the greeting and the body.\n- If the output does not start with \"Subject:\", FIX it before returning.\n- The `Subject:` keyword MUST be translated to the LanguageCode: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}  \n- Example:\n  - English: Subject:\n  - Arabic: الموضوع:\n  - German: Betreff:\n- The Email length MUST be ≤ {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.responseLimit}}\n\n#### When currentMode is \"Message\":\n- You MUST NOT include a subject line.\n- You MUST NOT include:\n  - Greetings (e.g., Hi, Hello, Dear)\n  - Recipient names\n  - Closings or sign-offs (e.g., Regards, Thanks, Agent)\n- Start DIRECTLY with the message body.\n- End with the message body.\n- If any greeting, name, or sign-off appears, REMOVE it before returning.\n\n\n### 4. Content Focus\n- Focus ONLY on the userInput message:\n  {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- Do not introduce new topics.\n- Use past context only for facts.\n- Avoid special characters. Prefer simple conjunctions like \"and\" or \"or\".\n\n### 5. Translation STRICTNESS (CRITICAL)\n\nYou MUST translate **ALL visible text** into the target LanguageCode: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}} , including:\n- The subject keyword (e.g., Subject)\n- Names (e.g., Rahul)\n- Sender sign-off (e.g., Agent)\n- Greetings and closings\n\n- Do NOT leave any word untranslated  \n- Do NOT mix languages  \n- Personal names (e.g., Rajesh) MUST be preserved.\n- When the target language uses a different script, you MUST transliterate the name into the target script.\n- NEVER replace a name with generic terms like \"Customer\".\n- NEVER remove names.\n- NEVER translate names semantically.\n\n### 6. RESPONSE LENGTH ENFORCEMENT (CRITICAL – HARD STOP)\n\nThe maximum allowed output length is:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.responseLimit}}\n\nThis limit is measured in CHARACTERS, including:\n- Spaces\n- Line breaks\n- Subject line (if Email mode)\n\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT VALIDATION (YOU MUST SELF-CHECK)\n\nBefore finalizing output:\n\n### If {{$context.$variables.currentMode==\"Email\"}}:\n- Check that the first line starts with `Subject:`\n- The word `Subject:` should in the given  LanguageCode: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}  \n- Check that there is exactly one subject line.\n- Check that the subject is short and relevant.\n\n### If {{$context.$variables.currentMode==\"Message\"}}:\n- Check that:\n  - There is NO subject line\n  - There is NO greeting\n  - There is NO name\n  - There is NO sign-off\n  - The output starts immediately with the body text\n  - The output ends with the body text\n\n### For BOTH:\n- The output length MUST be ≤ {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.responseLimit}}. This is mandatory and non-negotiable.\n- If any rule is violated, you MUST revise the output before returning it.\n- Under no circumstances may you return a response that exceeds the limit or violates any rule.\n\n---\n\n### Output Language constraint (MANDATORY)\n- 1st priority: The output should be in language, according to this LanguageCode: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}, if provided.\n- 2nd priority: Honor the language of the input data/context only if the language code is missing or unsupported.\n\n---"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"output\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "enrichText"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ENRICHTEXT",
          "id": "1765256020857",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765256020858_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## PROMPT IS NOT DATA (CRITICAL)\n\nThis entire instruction block is SYSTEM CONTROL TEXT.\n\nIt is NEVER part of the output document.\n\nThe model must NEVER:\n- reproduce\n- quote\n- summarize\n- transform\n- or echo\n\nany part of this prompt.\n\nIf any text from this prompt appears in the output, it is an error and must be removed before returning the final response.\n\nOnly the user document provided in the INPUT section is allowed to appear in the output.\n\n\n---\n\n## TASK\n\nYou will receive a dynamic multi-line text input from:\n\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Text}}\n\nYour job is to process and transform this document according to the rules below.\n\n\n---\n\n## INPUT\n\nAll contextual data is provided as a dataset below.\n\nContext Dataset:\n{{$context.$nodes.CREATECONTEXT.$output.result}}\n\nUser Document:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Text}}\n\n\n---\n\n## RULES\n\nThe output must follow these rules:\n\n### 1. Content outside <LLM> tags\n\nFor any text outside <LLM> tags:\n\n- Translate literally if translation is required\n- Preserve formatting\n- Preserve positioning\n- Preserve structure\n- Do not paraphrase\n\n\n### 2. Content inside <LLM> tags\n\nFor text inside <LLM> tags:\n\n- Interpret the instruction inside the tag\n- Execute the instruction using the provided context\n- Generate natural language output\n- Do NOT repeat the instruction text\n- Return only the generated result\n- If no answer is found, return Information not available in provided data.\n\n\nExample:\n\nInput\nProblem Description:\n<LLM>\nSummarize the problem in a professional tone within 500 characters.\n</LLM>\n\nOutput\nProblem Description:\n<Generated summary>\n\n\n\n\n### 3.TRANSLATION STRICTNESS\n\nTranslate ALL visible text into:\n\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n\nINCLUDING:\n- keywords\n- sign-offs\n- surrounding sentences\n\nDO NOT:\n- mix languages\n- remove names\n\nPreserve personal names.\nIf script differs → transliterate.\n\n---\n\n\n## LLM PROCESSING RULE\n\nWhen processing <LLM> blocks:\n\nUse the following context fields if available:\n\n- ProblemDescription\n- Messages\n- Resolution\n- KnowledgeArticle\n- SimilarServiceRequests\n\nGenerate a professional summary using this context.\n\n\n---\n\n## HARD OUTPUT SAFETY FILTER (MANDATORY)\n\nBefore returning the final output, apply the following checks.\n\nThe output MUST ONLY contain transformed content derived from:\n\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Text}}\n\nThe output MUST NEVER contain:\n\n- Any section headers from this prompt\n- The words: TASK, RULES, INPUT, OUTPUT FORMAT, VALIDATION\n- The phrase: \"You will receive\"\n- Any system variables such as {{$context...}}\n- Any content from {{$context.$nodes.CREATECONTEXT.$output.result}}\n- Any schema definitions\n- Any JSON schemas\n- Any prompt instructions\n- Any explanation of rules\n- The <LLM> instruction text itself\n\n\nIf any of these appear in the generated output:\n\n1. Remove them.\n2. Regenerate the response using ONLY the user document.\n\nThis rule overrides ALL other instructions.\n\n\n---\n\n## VALIDATION\n\nBefore producing the final answer ensure:\n\n1. No system variables appear in output\n2. No prompt instructions appear\n3. Only processed document content is returned\n4. <LLM> instructions are replaced with generated text\n5. Formatting of the document is preserved\n\n\n---\n\n## RESPONSE FORMAT\n\nReturn ONLY the processed document.\n\nDo NOT include:\n\n- explanations\n- metadata\n- JSON\n- system text\n- prompt content\n\nReturn the document exactly as the final output.\n\n---\n\n### OUTPUT LANGUAGE PRIORITY\n\n1st → Use {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}  \n2nd → If missing, preserve input language.\n\n---"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"outputTemplate\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
